Description: Patina Desktop, a Wayland desktop environment written in Rust
 Patina is a Wayland compositor and desktop shell written in Rust. This
 pre-release provides the compositor, with floating windows, titlebars drawn
 by the compositor and DRM/KMS output, and the top panel. It adds a "Patina"
 session to the login screen and a patina-session command for starting it
 from a text console.
 .
 Not yet included: dock, launcher, notifications, quick settings, lock
 screen, and the Terminal, File Bin and Settings apps. Until the Terminal
 app exists, install a Wayland terminal such as foot to have something to
 run.
 .
 The LightDM login manager cannot start Wayland sessions; use GDM or SDDM,
 or run patina-session from a text console.
